Anti-Ragging Policy

The institution follows a zero-tolerance policy towards ragging.

Any student found involved in ragging may face:

* Suspension
* Expulsion
* Legal action

Students can report incidents confidentially to the Anti-Ragging Committee.

Emergency Contact:

* 1800-000-111

⸻

Code of Conduct

Students are expected to:

* Respect faculty, staff, and fellow students.
* Maintain discipline on campus.
* Wear valid ID cards at all times.
* Use campus resources responsibly.
* Follow academic integrity standards.

Students must not:

* Engage in ragging.
* Damage college property.
* Use unfair means during examinations.
* Participate in disruptive activities.

